      "id": 1,
      "text": "Brooksville began as Woodward's Crossroads, settled before 1800 by brothers William and Joel Woodward.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brooksville%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1839 the county seat moved from Augusta, and the town was renamed Brooksville after Senator David Brooks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://kyatlas.com/ky-brooksville.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The railroad first planned Brooksville, and a later gas boom drew factories that reshaped the town’s economy.",
